---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Weigh Easy - Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Weigh Easy - Private Weight Tracker iOS app."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/weigh-easy/privacy"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--text-secondary)] mb-12">Weigh Easy &middot; Effective October 22, 2026</p>

        <div class="space-y-8 text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">The Short Version</h2>
            <p>Weigh Easy does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data. Your weight, measurements, and progress photos stay on your device and nowhere else.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Data Storage</h2>
            <p>All weigh-ins, body measurements, goals, and settings are stored locally on your iPhone. Weigh Easy shares a summary of your latest weigh-in, trend and goal with its own widgets and with its Apple Watch app on your paired watch. No data is sent to any server, cloud service, or third party. There are no user accounts and no sign-up required.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Progress Photos</h2>
            <p>Progress photos you take or add in Weigh Easy are stored only in the app's private storage on your iPhone, protected by iOS Data Protection. They are not added to your photo library or iCloud, are never uploaded anywhere, and are not accessible to other apps. They are left out of your iPhone's iCloud and computer backups unless you turn on Include in backups in Weigh Easy's settings. You can lock them with Face ID. If you delete the app, your photos are deleted with it. Earlier versions of Weigh Easy saved progress photos to your photo library; with your permission, Weigh Easy copies them into the app and leaves the originals unchanged.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Apple Health</h2>
            <p class="mb-3">Weigh Easy can connect to Apple Health, but only if you turn it on and grant permission. It is entirely optional. If you turn it on:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-2">
              <li>Weigh-ins you add in Weigh Easy are saved to Apple Health as Weight (body mass)</li>
              <li>Weight from your smart scale or other apps is read from Apple Health so it shows in your trend</li>
              <li>Weigh Easy reads and writes no other Health data</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="mt-3">HealthKit data is governed by <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">Apple's privacy policy</a> and never leaves your device through Weigh Easy. If you don't allow access, the app works normally with local-only storage.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Analytics & Tracking</h2>
            <p>Weigh Easy contains no analytics frameworks, no ad SDKs, no tracking pixels, and no telemetry of any kind. We do not use any third-party services that collect data.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Network Usage</h2>
            <p>Weigh Easy makes no network requests and works entirely offline. When it copies a photo saved by an earlier version from your photo library, Apple's Photos framework may download the original from iCloud Photos if you use it. The only other network activity associated with the app is through the App Store for updates.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Children's Privacy</h2>
            <p>Weigh Easy does not knowingly collect any information from anyone, including children under the age of 13.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Changes to This Policy</h2>
            <p>If this policy changes, we will update this page with the new effective date. Since Weigh Easy collects no data, meaningful changes are unlikely.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-3">Contact</h2>
            <p>Questions about this policy? Email us at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
